Very cool that a chameleon can be tamed if its current form
is tame-able and that tameness continues after the next
shift.

> When a chameleon imitates a monster, does it gain all of that
> monster's powers? =A0(i.e., is it a true polymorph?)

In my experience all of the powers are gained including the
damage done by hits, so a chameleon in balrog form is
majorly nasty.  But chameleons continue to be easy to
kill so it appears to me that they don't get the hit points of
the monster they appear to be.  This makes a chameleon
at the same time very nasty strength and near popcorn
weakness.  Quite bizarre and very classic Nethack.

> Seems like it could be a useful pet. =A0Sure, part of the time you'd
> have a newt, but part of the time you'd have an arch-lich...

While a mean monster it would do a lot of damage but no
matter the time it remains easy to kill.  Useful but short
lived pet - It takes out a watchman in the mines in one bite
then attacks the watch captain who just barely survives
the first bite and swings at the chameleon.  One swing is
enough and the chameleon dies.

